      "hints": [
        "For each flight, equate the kinetic energy at ground level to the change in gravitational potential energy at the turning point.",
        "Form h₂ / h₁ after writing the two energy equations; the common factors m and g cancel."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For the fall from height h₁, ½m(5.2)² = mgh₁, so h₁ = 5.2² / (2g) = 1.38 m.",
        "For the rebound to height h₂, ½m(3.6)² = mgh₂, so h₂ = 3.6² / (2g) = 0.66 m.",
        "The ratio is h₂ / h₁ = 0.66 / 1.38 = (3.6 / 5.2)² = 0.48."
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "deterministic_checks": [],
